-------------\nGröbner Bases for Fusion Products | Algebras and Representation Theory | Springer Nature Link (https://doi.org/10.1007/s10468-022-10179-6?urlappend=%3Futm_source%3Dresearchgate.net%26utm_medium%3Darticle)\nciteturn9search3 [wordlim: 200] Published: 4.0 years ago; Crawled: 2 months ago; We understand the fusion product as a degeneration using Gröbner theory of non-commutative algebras and outline a strategy on how to prove a conjecture about the defining relations for the fusion product of two evaluation modules. ... Chari, V., Fourier, G., Sagaki, D.: Posets, tensor products and Schur positivity.\n\n# Gröbner Bases for Fusion Products\n\n  * Open access\n  * Published: 28 October 2022\n\n  * Volume 26, pages 2235–2253 (2023)\n  * Cite this article\n\nYou have full access to this open access article\n\nDownload PDF\n\nSave article\n\nView saved research\n\nAlgebras and Representation Theory Aims and scope Submit manuscript\n\nGröbner Bases for Fusion Products\n\nDownload PDF\n\n  * Johannes Flake^{1},\n  * Ghislain Fourier  ORCID: orcid.org/0000-0002-1323-9200^{1} &\n  * Viktor Levandovskyy^{2} \n\n  * 620 Accesses\n\n  * Explore all metrics\n\n## Abstract\n\nWe provide a new approach towards the analysis of the fusion products defined by B. Feigin and S. Loktev in the representation theory of (truncated) current Lie algebras. We understand the fusion product as a degeneration using Gröbner theory of non-commutative algebras and outline a strategy on how to prove a conjecture about the defining relations for the fusion product of two evaluation modules. We conclude with following this strategy for $\\mathfrak {sl}_2(\\mathbb {C}[t]) $ and hence provide yet another proof for the conjecture in this case.\n\n## Article PDF\n\nArticle PDF\n\nDownload to read the full article text\n\n## Data Availability\n\nData sharing not applicable to this article as no datasets were generated or analysed during the current study.\n\n## References\n\n  1. Bianchi, A.,